{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Wherefore should they say, etc.</b> Meaning, this constitutes a profanation of the Name, for the Egyptians will say: Yesterday He said (Exodus 4:22) ״בְּנִי בְכוֹרִי יִשְׂרָאֵל … שְׁלַח … וְיַעַבְדֵנִי״, and now He has revealed His end to be contrary to His beginning — that He did not intend it for good, and Heaven forbid, He appears as a liar. Further, He thereby intends a known matter, that Israel serve HaShem and all the nations serve other forms of worship; and from what they will see — that HaShem brought them out for evil, something He did not do to those who worship other than Him — if so, Heaven forbid, a great blemish is manifest upon the servants of HaShem, and the hands of idol worshippers will be strongly strengthened, such that they have a claim." "And the verse's saying the word <b>לֵאמֹר</b> [saying]: it is not necessary that they say the words exactly as they are, in their order, but they will say things of which this is their intent. Or it may mean that the words are not true — Heaven forbid — but only in the aspect of 'saying.' Further it intends that not Egypt alone will say, but they will say and broadcast the words to everyone, for thereby — Heaven forbid — the profanation of the Name will be multiplied."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:35:54.874255623Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}